From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Make source generations reentrancy-safe.

Media engine source resolution can complete after a newer SetSource() call or
after shutdown. Give every Begin operation an explicit, refcounted origin and
generation context, always drain the matching End operation, and shut down
objects returned by stale completions.

The initial generation comparison is not sufficient because MediaEngine
notifications and old-source shutdown can reenter SetSource(), while
presentation cleanup deliberately drops the engine lock. Capture each
generation locally, revalidate it after PURGE, Begin, LOADSTART, and topology
cleanup, and detach the old presentation before dropping the lock. Pass the
generation through topology construction so an older callback cannot install
over a newer source.

Track the current Play/Pause intent independently while a source is loading,
and clear source/play pending flags when SetSource() receives no URL or byte
stream. Reject an out-of-memory URL copy needed by the asynchronous WineDMO
handler.

Non-shutdown MEError propagation remains deliberately deferred. This
quarantined candidate is not part of patches/series.

The license of each modified Wine source file applies to this patch.
